+# PLAN-012: Automatic reconnection for dropped STT provider sockets
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Context
+
+When the provider-side streaming socket (Deepgram or AssemblyAI) drops
+mid-session, the provider fires `onClose`, and `SessionManager.openStream`
+treats any non-paused, non-stopping close as fatal: it calls `finish(active)`
+and the transcription stream is lost for the rest of the session. The task:
+reconnect transparently up to 5 times with exponential backoff, buffer and
+flush audio across the gap, keep deliberate stop/shutdown from reconnecting,
+and surface a clear error through the existing event channel only after
+retries are exhausted.
+
+The codebase already composes cross-cutting stream behavior with provider
+decorators (`withIdleTimeout` in `server/stt/idle-timeout.ts`, applied in
+`createSTTProvider`), so reconnection is implemented the same way rather
+than inside `SessionManager` or duplicated per provider.
+
+## Governing records
+
+- ADR-002: STT is consumed only through the provider interface
+  (`start_stream` / `send_audio` / events); no provider SDK types leak into
+  application code. Reconnect therefore lives in a decorator over
+  `STTProvider`, not in manager or socket code. Billing hygiene: deepgram
+  bills per audio second, AssemblyAI per socket-open duration, so the
+  reconnect window must stay bounded (5 attempts, capped pending buffer,
+  existing idle timeout stays outermost).
+- ADR-006: no new dependencies; the decorator is plain TypeScript over the
+  existing interfaces, tests use vitest fake timers plus the existing
+  fake-socket harnesses.
+- BDR-001: real-time output is the product; reconnecting instead of ending
+  the session directly serves the real-time requirement.
+- BDR-002: cost ceiling; a bounded retry window plus the unchanged idle
+  timeout keep billed socket time proportional to real audio.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. `server/stt/reconnect.ts` (new): `withReconnect` provider decorator and
+   `SttReconnectError`.
+2. `server/stt/provider.ts`: one optional event added to `StreamEvents`.
+3. `server/stt/index.ts`: compose `withReconnect` inside `withIdleTimeout`
+   for both providers.
+4. `server/session/manager.ts`: rebase `streamBaseS` on reconnect via the
+   new event; pass `code` through on broadcast errors.
+5. `server/stt/reconnect.test.ts` (new): unit tests over a scripted inner
+   provider plus real providers driven by injected fake sockets.
+
+Out of scope:
+
+- Client-facing `/ws` resilience: `use-live-session.ts` already retries the
+  browser socket; unchanged.
+- Frontend changes of any kind. The exhausted-retry error travels the
+  existing `{ type: 'error' }` broadcast and lands in the existing toast.
+- Making retry parameters configurable via env (constants for now; see
+  Risks).
+- Mid-word partial recovery, sequence numbers, or gap-aware timestamp
+  repair (see Risks: buffered burst approximation).
+- Reconnect for the initial `start_stream` call: a first-connect failure
+  still rejects session start exactly as today.
+
+## Design decisions (pinned)
+
+### Decorator contract (`server/stt/reconnect.ts`, literal)
+
+```ts
+export interface ReconnectOptions {
+  maxAttempts?: number;      // default 5
+  baseDelayMs?: number;      // default 1000
+  stableMs?: number;         // default 5000
+  maxPendingChunks?: number; // default 512
+  random?: () => number;     // default Math.random; injected for tests
+}
+
+export class SttReconnectError extends Error {
+  readonly code = 'STT_RECONNECT_FAILED';
+  readonly attempts: number;
+  constructor(attempts: number, cause?: Error);
+}
+
+export function withReconnect(
+  provider: STTProvider,
+  opts?: ReconnectOptions,
+): STTProvider;
+```
+
+`SttReconnectError` message literal:
+`STT stream lost; reconnect failed after ${attempts} attempts`, with
+`cause` set to the last inner error when one exists. `name` is
+`'SttReconnectError'`.
+
+`withReconnect` returns an object exposing `name` and
+`supports_diarization` forwarded from the inner provider; `start_stream`
+returns an `STTStream` whose lifecycle is described below.
+
+### Event contract (`server/stt/provider.ts`, literal)
+
+```ts
+export interface StreamEvents {
+  onPartial(seg: Segment): void;
+  onFinal(seg: Segment): void;
+  onError(err: Error): void;
+  onClose?(): void;
+  onReconnect?(): void; // NEW: fired once per successful reconnection
+}
+```
+
+Optional field: existing providers, tests, and `withIdleTimeout` compile
+unchanged. `withIdleTimeout` spreads `...events` when wrapping, so
+`onReconnect` passes through it with no edit.
+
+### Stream state machine (per `start_stream` call)
+
+All state lives in the closure of one `start_stream` invocation; a new
+manager-level `openStream` (pause/resume, session start) gets fresh state.
+
+- `deliberate: boolean` starts false; `inner: STTStream | null`;
+  `pending: Buffer[]`; `attempts: number` (reconnect attempts made for the
+  current incident); `timer` for the pending attempt; `openedAt: number`
+  timestamp of the last healthy stream; `lastError: Error | undefined`;
+  `exhausted: boolean`.
+- The inner provider is started with wrapped events:
+  `onPartial`/`onFinal` forward straight through.
+- Inner `onError(err)`: store as `lastError`. If `deliberate`, forward to
+  `events.onError`. Otherwise treat exactly like an unexpected close:
+  call `inner.close()` to normalize (wrapped in try/catch) and enter the
+  reconnect flow. Rationale: requirement says "close or error"; `ws` and
+  the Deepgram SDK both emit `error` before `close`, and holding the error
+  (not forwarding it) means transient failures never reach the client
+  unless retries exhaust.
+- Inner `onClose()`: if `deliberate`, forward `events.onClose?.()`.
+  Otherwise enter the reconnect flow.
+- Reconnect flow: if the just-lost stream survived `>= stableMs`
+  (`Date.now() - openedAt >= stableMs`), reset `attempts` to 0 first (a new
+  incident). Then `scheduleAttempt()`.
+- `scheduleAttempt()`: if `attempts >= maxAttempts`, set `exhausted`,
+  emit `events.onError(new SttReconnectError(attempts, lastError))` then
+  `events.onClose?.()`, and stop. Otherwise increment `attempts` and set
+  `timer = setTimeout(connect, delayFor(attempts))`.
+- Delay formula (literal): for attempt `n` (1-based),
+  `delayFor(n) = baseDelayMs * 2 ** (n - 1) * random()` - full jitter over
+  [0, 1s/2s/4s/8s/16s) for the default base. Injected `random` makes tests
+  deterministic.
+- `connect()`: `provider.start_stream(opts, wrappedEvents)` again. On
+  resolve: assign `inner`, set `openedAt`, flush `pending` in order
+  through `inner.send_audio` (each call try/catch; a throw stops the flush
+  and leaves the rest queued... no: pin it - a throw stops the flush and
+  the remaining chunks are discarded, since the provider contract expects
+  `send_audio` not to throw and a throwing fresh stream is itself
+  unhealthy), then fire `events.onReconnect?.()`. On reject: store the
+  rejection as `lastError` and call `scheduleAttempt()` again (the reject
+  counts toward the same `attempts` budget; no `onClose` event is
+  involved).
+- Outer `send_audio(chunk)`: if `deliberate` or `exhausted`, drop
+  silently. If `inner` is null (mid-backoff or mid-connect), push to
+  `pending`; when `pending` is at `maxPendingChunks`, drop the oldest
+  chunk (FIFO shift) to bound memory. Otherwise forward to
+  `inner.send_audio` inside try/catch (provider contract says no throw,
+  but stay safe like `withIdleTimeout` does).
+- Outer `close()`: set `deliberate`, clear `timer`, clear `pending`, call
+  `inner?.close()` in try/catch. If no `onClose` has been forwarded yet,
+  forward `events.onClose?.()` once, so `close()` still produces the
+  close signal callers see today even when the socket was already dead or
+  a backoff was pending.
+
+The `stableMs` reset prevents infinite flap: a socket that dies within 5s
+of opening continues the same incident and burns the retry budget, while a
+long-lived stream that drops starts a fresh 5-attempt budget.
+
+### Composition order (`server/stt/index.ts`, literal shape)
+
+```ts
+return withIdleTimeout(
+  withReconnect(new AssemblyAIProvider(config.ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY)),
+  config.STT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S,
+);
+// and likewise withReconnect(new DeepgramProvider(config.DEEPGRAM_API_KEY))
+```
+
+`withReconnect` MUST be innermost. The idle decorator's timeout fires
+`events.onError(IdleTimeoutError)` and then closes its inner stream; if
+the reconnect wrapper sat outside, that deliberate inner close would read
+as an unexpected drop and resurrect the stream, silently defeating the
+idle timeout. With idle outermost, its `close()` reaches the wrapper's
+`close()`, which sets `deliberate` and never reconnects. During a backoff
+gap, incoming audio still flows through idle's `send_audio` (resetting its
+timer) into the wrapper's pending buffer, so continuous speech does not
+idle-kill a session mid-reconnect; a genuinely silent 30s gap can still
+time out, which is consistent with billing hygiene.
+
+### Manager changes (`server/session/manager.ts`)
+
+- Extract the existing openStream base computation into
+  `private unpausedElapsedS(active: ActiveSession): number` (the exact
+  expression already inline in `openStream`), use it at openStream entry,
+  and reuse it for the rebase below.
+- `openStream` events gain
+  `onReconnect: () => { active.streamBaseS = this.unpausedElapsedS(active); }`.
+  Provider timestamps restart at 0 on each new socket; without the rebase,
+  `[mm:ss]` tags would regress mid-session. With it, post-reconnect
+  segments continue at wall-clock session time (the gap-burst caveat is in
+  Risks).
+- `handleSttError`: after the `IdleTimeoutError` branch, broadcast with a
+  code passthrough:
+  `{ type: 'error', message: err.message, ...(((err as { code?: string }).code) ? { code: (err as { code?: string }).code } : {}) }`
+  so `STT_RECONNECT_FAILED` reaches the client as a coded error event.
+- The `onClose` handler (`finish` on unexpected close) is unchanged: with
+  the wrapper, the manager only sees `onClose` for deliberate closes
+  (ignored via `stopping`/`paused`) or after retry exhaustion (finishes
+  the session, which is correct once the stream is unrecoverable).
+
+### Why a decorator, not manager-side reconnect (recorded decision)
+
+Manager-side retry would reuse `openStream` and get `streamBaseS` for
+free, but it pushes retry timers, pending buffers, and attempt state into
+an already-large `ActiveSession`, duplicates what `withIdleTimeout` proves
+is the codebase's composition style, and is harder to cover with the
+required mocked-socket tests. The decorator needs only the optional
+`onReconnect` event added to the contract.
+
+## Steps
+
+### Step 1 - `server/stt/provider.ts`
+
+Add `onReconnect?(): void` to `StreamEvents` (literal above). No other
+change; the contract harness in `contract.ts` is untouched.
+
+### Step 2 - `server/stt/reconnect.ts` (new)
+
+Implement `SttReconnectError`, `ReconnectOptions`, and `withReconnect`
+per the pinned state machine, delay formula, buffer bounds, and event
+semantics above. Defaults: `maxAttempts` 5, `baseDelayMs` 1000,
+`stableMs` 5000, `maxPendingChunks` 512, `random` = `Math.random`.
+
+### Step 3 - `server/stt/index.ts`
+
+Wrap both provider constructions in `withReconnect` inside
+`withIdleTimeout` (literal shape above).
+
+### Step 4 - `server/session/manager.ts`
+
+Extract `unpausedElapsedS`, add the `onReconnect` handler in `openStream`,
+add the `code` passthrough in `handleSttError`. No new fields on
+`ActiveSession`; no change to `sendAudio`, `pause`, `resume`, `stop`,
+`finish`.
+
+### Step 5 - `server/stt/reconnect.test.ts` (new)
+
+Cases listed in the test plan below.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Automated (vitest), all offline - provider keys are test strings and every
+socket is a fake injected through `connectFn`/`wsFactory` or a scripted
+inner provider:
+
+- Scripted inner provider (a FakeProvider in the `idle-timeout.test.ts`
+  style, extended to capture `events` and expose `startCount`, scripted to
+  let the test emit `close`/`error`/`open` and to reject `start_stream` on
+  demand), wrapped in `withReconnect`:
+  - unexpected `close` triggers exactly one `start_stream` retry;
+    `onClose` is NOT forwarded to outer events on transient drops.
+  - `vi.useFakeTimers()` with `random: () => 0.5`: attempts land at 0.5,
+    1, 2, 4, 8s after each failure (delay = base * 2^(n-1) * 0.5); a 6th
+    attempt is never made.
+  - after 5 failed attempts: outer `onError` receives an
+    `SttReconnectError` with `code === 'STT_RECONNECT_FAILED'`, then outer
+    `onClose` fires once.
+  - audio sent while `inner` is null is buffered and flushed in order to
+    the replacement stream; buffer overflow drops oldest, not newest.
+  - outer `close()` during backoff: timer cleared, no further
+    `start_stream` calls, `onClose` forwarded once. `close()` after
+    exhaustion is a no-op beyond the single forwarded close.
+  - a stream surviving `>= stableMs` before dropping resets the attempt
+    budget (drop -> 5s+ open -> drop starts a fresh attempt 1).
+  - a rejected `start_stream` during reconnect consumes an attempt and
+    reschedules; outer `onError` is not called until exhaustion.
+- Mocked-socket coverage through the real providers (literal "mocked
+  socket" requirement, zero network):
+  - `withReconnect(new DeepgramProvider('test-key', connectFn))` where
+    `connectFn` resolves successive `FakeDgSocket`s: socket1 `emit('close')`
+    mid-stream -> `connectFn` called again -> buffered audio flushes to
+    socket2's `sendMedia` on its `open`.
+  - `withReconnect(new AssemblyAIProvider('test-key', wsFactory))` with a
+    `FakeWs` sequence: first socket `emit('close')` -> factory called
+    again -> second socket `emit('open')` -> pending audio flushes via
+    `send`.
+- `server/app.test.ts`: no changes required; the injected
+  `providerFactory` bypasses `createSTTProvider`, so the existing
+  FakeProvider keeps its current "unexpected close finishes the session"
+  semantics. Optionally add one regression test later; not part of this
+  plan's DoD.
+- Gates: `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` (the task's stated gates).
+
+Manual acceptance (post-implementation, needs real keys; not a DoD gate):
+
+- Start a session on Deepgram, kill outbound connectivity ~10s, restore:
+  transcription resumes, `[mm:ss]` tags do not regress, no error toast.
+- Stop during a forced outage: session ends immediately, no reconnect
+  attempts in logs.
+- With connectivity dead past ~31s of backoff: a single error toast
+  (`STT_RECONNECT_FAILED`) and the session ends.
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- **Assumption: decorator layer.** "The STT websocket" is read as the
+  provider-side socket inside the `STTProvider` abstraction; the
+  client-facing `/ws` socket already retries in `use-live-session.ts`.
+- **Assumption: error == drop.** Any inner `onError` triggers the
+  reconnect flow, per the requirement's "close or error". Neither current
+  adapter emits recoverable-only errors, so no false-positive churn is
+  expected; if a provider later adds non-fatal warnings, this rule may
+  need a severity check.
+- **Buffered burst skews timestamps.** Audio captured during the gap is
+  flushed as a burst; the provider stamps it with post-open stream time,
+  so those segments compress the gap. `streamBaseS` rebase keeps later
+  segments monotonic; exact gap-aware timing needs sequence numbers, out
+  of scope.
+- **Silent-gap idle race.** Max backoff sum is ~31s worst case (~15.5s
+  average under full jitter). A reconnect gap with zero audio can hit the
+  30s idle timeout first and end the session with `IDLE_TIMEOUT`. Accepted
+  as billing hygiene (ADR-002): no billable stream exists during the gap
+  anyway, and speech resets the timer.
+- **Constants, not config.** Retry parameters are constructor-injectable
+  constants, not env vars - proportional documentation for a single-site
+  policy. Promote to `Config` only if operators ask for tuning.
+- **Buffer bound.** 512 chunks is a rough bound (at the worklet's
+  ~20-100ms cadence it covers more than the worst-case backoff window);
+  overflow drops oldest so a long outage loses the earliest gap audio
+  rather than unbounded memory.
+- **First connect is not retried.** `start_stream` rejection on session
+  start still fails the start - deliberate, since a dead provider at t=0
+  is a config/credential problem the user should see immediately.
+- **No frontend change.** The client already renders `{type:'error'}`
+  broadcasts as toasts; `STT_RECONNECT_FAILED` flows through the same
+  channel.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `withReconnect` in `server/stt/reconnect.ts` implements the pinned
+      state machine: unexpected close/error schedules up to 5 retries at
+      `baseDelayMs * 2^(n-1) * random()`; `stableMs` resets the incident
+      budget; pending audio is bounded at `maxPendingChunks` (drop-oldest)
+      and flushed in order on the replacement stream; `onReconnect` fires
+      after a successful reconnect.
+- [ ] Deliberate `close()` (including pause/stop/shutdown paths) cancels
+      any pending retry and never reconnects.
+- [ ] After 5 failed attempts the outer events see one
+      `SttReconnectError` (`code: 'STT_RECONNECT_FAILED'`) followed by one
+      `onClose`, which ends the session through the existing manager path.
+- [ ] `StreamEvents.onReconnect` added; `createSTTProvider` composes
+      `withIdleTimeout(withReconnect(provider))` for both providers.
+- [ ] Manager rebases `streamBaseS` on `onReconnect` and forwards `code`
+      on error broadcasts.
+- [ ] `server/stt/reconnect.test.ts` covers every case in the test plan
+      using scripted inner providers and injected fake sockets only; no
+      test touches the real network or real provider keys.
+- [ ] `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` pass.
-- 
